Subject: [PATCH 2/3] =?UTF-8?q?cranelift:=20Lower::sink=5Fpure=5Finst=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20absorb=20pure=20ALU=20ops=20into=20terminators?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a public Lower API to mark a non-side-effecting CLIF instruction as
"absorbed" by a later-emitted MachInst — typically a terminator that
fuses an ALU op with a branch. The absorbing MachInst must write to the
absorbed inst's result vreg directly so subsequent put_value_in_regs
calls (e.g. block-call-arg machinery) observe the correct value. The
absorbed inst is then skipped in lower_clif_block, preventing a
redundant second write to the same vreg (which would violate SSA
single-def).

Distinct from sink_inst, which is for side-effecting insts and asserts
no remaining lowered uses. sink_pure_inst is for pure ALU ops whose
value-production flows into the fused MachInst's output operand. It is
the missing piece for emitting "compute + branch" MachInsts where the
ALU op's result has additional uses (e.g. as a block-call argument)
beyond the fused branch's cond test.

Motivation: the Pulley Cranelift backend's `xband + brif` fusion at
call_indirect sites needs to absorb the band's pure value-production
into the new BandBrIf MachInst's dst, while the band's result is
simultaneously consumed as a block-call argument by the standard branch
lowering machinery. sink_inst doesn't apply because the band is pure;
without sink_pure_inst the band would lower a second time and double-
write the vreg.
